# Regression: menu open/close leaves no native-pixel stamp where the dropdown was.
# Motivating bug (Phase 2 checkpoints): closing the game menu used to leave blocky
# native pixels where a dropdown had been. Two activation paths are exercised because
# they are DISTINCT SCI code paths and the original gate (ESC-only, top-band-only)
# missed the mouse-drag residue that reached deep into the scene:
#   1. ESC keyboard menu (interactiveWithKeyboard), and
#   2. mouse press-drag across the title bar (interactiveWithMouse) — the user's gesture.
# m-before vs m-after (ESC path) and d-before vs d-after (drag path) must be
# pixel-identical across the whole upper scene band the dropdowns overlap, not just the
# menu bar. QFG1 target, save slot 1 (room 300: dropdowns extend well into the scene).
wait 4000
capture m-before
# --- ESC keyboard path: open, walk across menus, close ---
key ESC
wait 1000
key RIGHT
wait 700
key RIGHT
wait 700
capture m-open
key ESC
wait 1200
move 160 100
wait 600
capture m-after
# --- mouse press-drag path: hold + drag across all titles + release in scene ---
move 160 100
wait 600
capture d-before
mousedown 20 3
wait 400
move 60 3
wait 400
move 110 3
wait 400
move 160 3
wait 400
move 210 3
wait 400
move 160 45
wait 400
move 160 120
wait 300
mouseup 160 120
wait 1400
move 160 100
wait 600
capture d-after
# move the mouse over the residue band: a real stamp is NOT healed by mouse-over
move 130 34
wait 500
move 160 100
wait 600
capture d-afterhover
wait 400
quit
